  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1255 AM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nThursday night...An H7 closed low over south central SD into north \ncentral NE will drop southeast into the Mid Missouri Valley by 12Z \nFriday. This will bring chance POPs across the area during the \nevening, and the eastern zones after midnight. Model consensus is \nfor most of the measurable rainfall will be across north central NE. \nNBM 12hr hour probabilities for greater than 0.10 inch is only from \n25 to 40 percent east of Callaway through Bassett. Areas to the west \nlook drier with only a 5 to 15 percent probability.   \n\nFriday...The upper ridge center will intensity over the Four Corner \nRegion as upper ridging builds back into Nebraska. Sunny with light \nsouth to southwest winds 5 to 10 mph. Highs reach 92 to 96 west of \nHighway 83, with 85 to 90 in the east. With dewpoints near 65, heat \nindices reach 90 to around 95, making outdoor activities unpleasant. \n \nSaturday through Tuesday...The upper ridge will remain centered from \nColorado through Oklahoma, with upper ridging extending north into \nthe Northern Plains.  Mainly dry conditions, although isolated \nthunderstorms are possible. H7 temperatures around 18 to around 20C \nSaturday warm to around 20C Sunday through Monday. Mainly dry \nconditions, although isolated storms appear possible during the late \nafternoon and evening hours through Tuesday, despite the warm \ntemperatures aloft. \n\nHot temperatures are also likely. NBM probability of exceeding 100 \ndegrees is from 60 to 90 percent across north central NE, the \nwestern Sandhills and southwest for both Saturday and Sunday with \nforecast highs from the upper 90s to low 100s. Highs Monday are \nlikely to remain hot in the upper 90s, with around 100 possible. \nHighs may lower a bit Tuesday into the low to mid 90s, as an upper \ntrough moves across the Great Lakes with a weak cold front through \nNebraska.",
